    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that \"balanced\" thing sounds good in theory but it's hard to actually do. if you try to do both at the same time, don't you risk watering down the truth? like, if you spend half the time on \"triumphs\" you're basically just glossing over the bad stuff that actually happened. wouldn't a curriculum that prioritizes systemic injustice be more honest and effective for teaching students how the world actually works?",
